FWIW, I'm going to quote Wikipedia's entry on nethack to you. The second
paragraph reads:

The "net" element references that its development has been coordinated
through the Internet.[4] The "hack" element refers to a genre of
role-playing games known as hack and slash for their focus on combat. The
player takes the part of a dungeon-delving character in search of the
Amulet of Yendor.[5]

Notice a couple of things.  First, they identify it as a "role-playing 
game," implying that they're using a definition which includes nethack.
Second, they say what role the player actually plays - so clearly they 
think that nethack is a game where you play a role, too. 

I consider this an example of majority usage. But then I wouldn't be 
surprised to see Mario Bros. described as a roleplaying game too. 
 
